    "login": "jmanico",
    "name": "Jim Manico"
  },
  "body": "The most recent language in 6.2.6 implies that only one IV should be used per key. Just to be clear we really should state that an IV should be used once per key/data-element pair, not just once per key. That's way, way too aggressive.\r\n\r\nFrom https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/blob/master/5.0/en/0x14-V6-Cryptography.md\r\n\r\n6.2.6 | Verify that nonces, initialization vectors, and other single use numbers must not be used more than once with a given encryption key. The method of generation must be appropriate for the algorithm being used. |   | ✓ | ✓ | 326\r\n-- | -- | -- | -- | -- | --\r\n\r\n\r\n",
